{"name":"Bear Claw","hex":"#ae6b52","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bear claw","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, sweet pastry filled with raisins and spices."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bear_claw"}],"entries":[{"title":"Claw","blocks":[{"text":"A claw is a curved, pointed appendage found at the end of a toe or finger in most amniotes. Some invertebrates such as beetles, spiders, and velvet worms have somewhat similar fine, hooked structures at the end of the leg or tarsus for gripping a surface as they walk. The pincers of crabs, lobsters, crayfish, shrimps, prawns and scorpions, more formally known as their chelae, are sometimes called claws."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Cat_claw_closeup.jpg/330px-Cat_claw_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claw","wikidata":"Q217605"},{"title":"Bear claw","blocks":[{"text":"A bear claw is a sweet pastry originating in the United States during the mid-1910s. The name bear claw as used for a pastry is first attested in a 1914 newspaper ad for the Geibel German Bakery in Sacramento, California."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Bear_claw_pastry.JPG/330px-Bear_claw_pastry.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_claw","wikidata":"Q871619"},{"title":"Bear","blocks":[{"text":"Bears are carnivoran mammals of the family Ursidae. They are classified as caniforms within the suborder Caniformia. Although only eight species of bears are extant, they are widespread, appearing in a wide variety of habitats throughout most of the Northern Hemisphere and partially in the Southern Hemisphere. Bears are found on the continents of North America, South America, and Eurasia. Common characteristics of modern bears include large bodies with stocky legs, long snouts, small rounded ears, shaggy hair, plantigrade paws with five nonretractile claws, and short tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg/330px-Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear","wikidata":"Q11788"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Cat_claw_closeup.jpg/500px-Cat_claw_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Cat_claw_closeup.jpg/1280px-Cat_claw_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Cat_claw_closeup.jpg/500px-Cat_claw_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A domestic cat's retractable claw in protracted position","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACat_claw_closeup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Therizinosaurus_claw.jpg/500px-Therizinosaurus_claw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Therizinosaurus_claw.jpg/1280px-Therizinosaurus_claw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Therizinosaurus_claw.jpg/500px-Therizinosaurus_claw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"At just under   a meter, the claws of Therizinosaurus are among the largest recorded.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATherizinosaurus_claw.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Grenn_lizzard.jpg/500px-Grenn_lizzard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t